## V2 architecture & layout (authoritative)

### Layout
- `publisher_v2/src/publisher_v2/app.py`: CLI entrypoint and orchestration wiring
- `publisher_v2/src/publisher_v2/config/loader.py`: config loading and validation
- `publisher_v2/src/publisher_v2/config/schema.py`: Pydantic v2 config models
- `publisher_v2/src/publisher_v2/core/`: exceptions, domain models, workflow orchestrator
- `publisher_v2/src/publisher_v2/services/`: AI, storage (Dropbox), publishers
- `publisher_v2/src/publisher_v2/utils/`: captions, images, logging, preview, rate_limit, state
- `publisher_v2/src/publisher_v2/web/`: FastAPI app, auth helpers, web service layer, templates

Keep new modules consistent with this layout; **do not create parallel V2 trees**.

### Orchestration boundaries
- Orchestration lives in `WorkflowOrchestrator` (`publisher_v2.core.workflow`).
- Platform logic belongs in publishers (`publisher_v2.services.publishers.*`) implementing the `Publisher` interface.

### AI integration
- Use `AIService` composed of `VisionAnalyzerOpenAI` and `CaptionGeneratorOpenAI`.
- For vision analysis use OpenAI chat completions with `response_format={"type": "json_object"}`.
- Enforce rate limits via `AsyncRateLimiter` (keep defaults unless asked to change).

### Storage
- Dropbox is the source of truth; prefer server-side moves to archive.

### Recording decisions
- Architecturally significant decisions (new module boundary, new external dependency/datastore,
  backward-incompatible contract change) get an ADR in `docs_v2/03_Architecture/adr/` via
  `/product-adr`. See `docs_v2/03_Architecture/adr/README.md` for when one is warranted.

